    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493296637/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """finally settled into harness with his  Michelangelo . The weather has been lovely. Janet Dodge has been here, goes next Wednesday. I can’t think of anything special we have said, except that Bernhard, in answer to the Mortons’ gibe that Englishmen lacked humour said, “Yes, they are noted for a lack of  American  humour.” He describes Arthur Symonds as “drippings of George Moore”.
Horne is here, and we went to the Villa  Salviati  with him. I’ve also visited  Castello ,  Petraia  and I  Collazzi .
no entries until 
Sunday Oct. 28. 1900. Frullino Florence
Mr. Ross had another stroke on Tuesday and lost his speech for two days. I have been there every day since, and once I have seen him. He is recovering marvellously. I get fonder of them all every day. The only other special events of this week """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 133 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1899-02> .

